2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]     # After validation and route analysis, it classifies the delivery:
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]     # - light deliveries have weight up to 5 kg;
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]     # - heavier deliveries are classified as heavy;
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]     # - fragile deliveries over long distances require special handling;
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]     # - routes with many checkpoints receive a long-route suffix.
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]     
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]     def classify_delivery(weight_kg: int, distance_km: int, fragile: bool) -> str:
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]         """
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]         Returns a simple classification for a delivery request.
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]     
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]         Rules:
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]         - weight_kg must be >= 0
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]         - distance_km must be >= 0
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]         - fragile indicates whether the package needs extra care
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]         - distance is analyzed through a small loop that counts 50 km checkpoints
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]         """
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]     
2026-05-14 00:20:53 [AutoTesting]         # Validate the basic input domain.
